monsterpop wrote:
> ok, so i have a pretty good game going. my best yet, actually; shunji
> the samurai has successfully completed the quest & has just entered
> dlvl 27 which seems to contain a castle of sorts. i have the following
> artifacts available: +3 snickersnee, +4 excalibur, +0 frost brand, +0
> fire brand & +0 tsurugi of muramasa. i have been using excalibur & a +3
> katana till now. is that a good choice? i reckon the tsurugi is
> 2-handed, and i have no slots to advance that. does it have some
> additional effect to the luckstone? would fire/frost brand protect my
> scrolls & potions?

Your best all-around combination is probably Excalibur and a katana.
Enchant both to +7 and make certain to advance both longsword and
twoweapon skills to expert.  Snickersnee does almost as much damage as
Excalibur, but doesn't get some of the nicer side effects ... keep it
handy as a back-up in case something happens to Excalibur (enchantment
accident, theft, etc).  The two foo-brands don't have "always on"
damage bonuses, and many of the nastier monsters resist one or both,
negating the double damage.  Given what you've got handy, the Tsurugi
is best stuffed away in a container.

> also, i recently gave up +1 gauntlets of power for +3 yugake. my
> "normal" strength is 18/62, but i'm also a part-time vampire lord with
> 18/**. should i go for strength or AC? (human AC is @ about -19)

Go for AC, and snack on giants until your strength gets up to 18/**.

> also also, i've been switching between +3 cloak of protection & +0
> cloak of displacement. which one would YOU choose? i'm thinking
> protection for the moment.

Neither, I'd use either a robe (if you have GDSM) or a Cloak of Magic
resistance (if you have SDSM).  In the interim stick with the AC
granted by the cloak of protection.

